# Intentionally empty.
#
# There is no .env in this project: configuration comes from the container
# environment (docker compose), and phpunit.xml sets what the test run needs.
#
# This file exists only so Laravel has an environment file to load when
# APP_ENV=testing. Without it, LoadEnvironmentVariables falls back to probing
# for .env, which is absent — and every single test carried a
# "file_get_contents(.env): No such file or directory" warning from
# vendor/vlucas/phpdotenv, drowning out the warnings that matter.
#
# Do not put values here. Anything the tests need belongs in phpunit.xml,
# where it sits next to the rest of the test configuration and cannot drift
# away from what CI and the containers actually use.
